4	// `compare` entry. These tests pin behaviour end to end on the in-package
5	// API: the archived side keeps the version that judged it at archive time,
6	// the candidate side is judged strictly under the version named in the
7	// call (never the currently enabled one), diffs are split per victim
8	// transaction, ordering and evidence are preserved, the query is read
9	// only, and pre-version legacy archives are interpreted as builtin.
